<< /AP << /D 951 0 R /N 952 0 R >> /C [ 0.25 0.333328 1 ] /Contents (ELGlN \rWhen the CP Rail Operator at Tower B17 routes a WWD Metra Train on No. 2 MT between Tower B35 and Elgin, the Operator will advise the location of any WWD CP Rail freight trains operating between Tower B17 and Tower B35. \r\rWhen so advised of a closely following CP Rail freight train, the Metra Engineer will notify his Train Crew who will protect the pedestrian crosswalk at Elgin Depot to prevent detraining passengers from crossing the No. 1 MT in front of the approaching freight train. Crosswalk will be protected until detraining passengers can safely cross No.1 MT or the crosswalk is occupied by the freight train.\r\rDuring inclement weather, Conductor of "Off-Peak" trains at Elgin will arrange to allow passengers to board and detrain at the coach nearest to the station. If the coach nearest to the station is not "In-Service", passengers will be allowed to use that coach to board and detrain and should be politely directed to walk through the train to or from the "In-Service" coach\(e\220s\). \r\rAdditionally, "Off-Peak" trains WILL NOT be left blocking the pedestrian crosswalk. \r) /CreationDate (D:20080917173712-05'00') /F 156 /M (D:20080917173746-05'00') /NM (df8461b3-167a-4376-8747-c36b06815a83) /Name /Comment /P 51 0 R /Popup 839 0 R /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt;font-weight:bold">ELGlN &#13;</span><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt">When the CP Rail Operator at Tower B17 routes a WWD Metra Train on No. 2 MT between Tower B35 and Elgin, the Operator will advise the location of any WWD CP Rail freight trains operating between Tower B17 and Tower B35. &#13;&#13;When so advised of a closely following CP Rail freight train, the Metra Engineer will notify his Train Crew who will protect the pedestrian crosswalk at Elgin Depot to prevent detraining passengers from crossing the No. 1 MT in front of the approaching freight train. Crosswalk will be protected until detraining passengers can safely cross No.1 MT or the crosswalk is occupied by the freight train.&#13;&#13;During inclement weather, Conductor of &quot;Off-Peak&quot; trains at Elgin will arrange to allow passengers to board and detrain at the coach nearest to the station. If the coach nearest to the station is not &quot;In-Service&quot;, passengers will be allowed to use that coach to board and detrain and should be politely directed to walk through the train to or from the &quot;In-Service&quot; coach\(e&#8217;s\). &#13;&#13;Additionally, &quot;Off-Peak&quot; trains WILL NOT be left blocking the pedestrian crosswalk. &#13;</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 205.531 399.295 225.531 417.295 ] /Rotate 270 /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot >>
endobj
839 0 obj
<< /F 156 /Open false /Parent 838 0 R /Rect [ 322.001 286.854 935.5 549.354 ] /Subtype /Popup /Type /Annot >>
endobj
840 0 obj
<< /AP << /D 951 0 R /N 952 0 R >> /C [ 0.25 0.333328 1 ] /Contents (Additional instructions\r\rMetra trains initiating EWD movement on No. 2 MT at Elgin, which have not made EWD movement on signal indication by the EWD absolute signal at MP 36.7 \(Chicago St.\), must obtain permission from the control operator at Tower B17 before making EWD movement from Elgin to the EWD absolute signal, on cantilever bridge, at MP 36.3. \r\rAfter obtaining permission, EWD movement must be made at restricted speed prepared to stop short of men or equipment until the leading wheels have passed the next governing signal. \r\rWhen no operator is on duty at Elgin, conductors of Metra trains must report the arrival time of their train to the train dispatcher at the stations indicated in accordance with the following instructions: \r\rElgin\r\rConductors of metra trains terminating at Elgin must report the arrival time of their train at Elgin to the train dispatcher when no operator is on duty.\r) /CreationDate (D:20080917173854-05'00') /F 156 /M (D:20080917174254-05'00') /NM (2dc40d3c-907d-48b4-84bf-9781b2ee0116) /Name /Comment /P 51 0 R /Popup 841 0 R /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt">Additional instructions&#13;&#13;Metra trains initiating EWD movement on No. 2 MT at Elgin, which have not made EWD movement on signal indication by the EWD absolute signal at MP 36.7 \(Chicago St.\), must obtain permission from the control operator at Tower B17 before making EWD movement from Elgin to the EWD absolute signal, on cantilever bridge, at MP 36.3. &#13;&#13;After obtaining permission, EWD movement must be made at restricted speed prepared to stop short of men or equipment until the leading wheels have passed the next governing signal. &#13;&#13;When no operator is on duty at Elgin, conductors of Metra trains must report the arrival time of their train to the train dispatcher at the stations indicated in accordance with the following instructions: &#13;&#13;Elgin&#13;&#13;Conductors of metra trains terminating at Elgin must report the arrival time of their train at Elgin to the train dispatcher when no operator is on duty.&#13;</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 379.617 537.849 399.617 555.849 ] /Rotate 270 /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot >>
endobj
