860 0 obj
<< /AP << /D 951 0 R /N 952 0 R >> /C [ 0.25 0.333328 1 ] /Contents (Big Timber Road\r\rConductors of Metra trains Nos. 2253, 2255 and 2257, must report the arrival time of their train at Big Timber Rd. To the train dispatcher upon arrival of eastward equipment movement at Elgin. \r\rTrain Nos. 2253, 2255 and 2257, may terminate at Elgin instead of Big Timber Road when there are no passengers for Big Timber Road. When terminating at Elgin, the control operator at Tower B17 must be so notified. \r\rWhen no operator is on duty, conductors of Metra trains required to receive a TGBO at Elgin must ascertain from the train dispatcher that they have all required track bulletins before their train departs Elgin. \r\rThe train dispatcher is to be contacted sufficiently in advance of departure time to avoid train delay should it be necessary to receive a new TGBO and track bulletins. \r\rWWD midday trains turning at Big Timber Road, beginning with train No. 2209 and continuing through train No. 2219, after making station stop will proceed west approximately one-half \(1/2\) the distance to Randall Road. \r\rEWD trains will proceed to the station platform and spot train for boarding not less than fifteen \(15\) minutes prior to scheduled departure. EWD trains using No. 2 MT will arrange to leave crosswalk clear and \(if deadheading cars\) load the second car from the east end, thereby allowing passengers to utilize the crosswalk and board the train. \r) /CreationDate (D:20080917174110-05'00') /F 156 /M (D:20080917174154-05'00') /NM (7c6141e1-0878-448c-8bae-3023f4a06e5c) /Name /Comment /P 52 0 R /Popup 861 0 R /RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:7.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt;font-weight:bold">Big Timber Road&#13;</span><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt;color:#FF0000;font-weight:bold">&#13;</span><span style="text-decoration:;font-size:12.0pt">Conductors of Metra trains Nos. 2253, 2255 and 2257, must report the arrival time of their train at Big Timber Rd. To the train dispatcher upon arrival of eastward equipment movement at Elgin. &#13;&#13;Train Nos. 2253, 2255 and 2257, may terminate at Elgin instead of Big Timber Road when there are no passengers for Big Timber Road. When terminating at Elgin, the control operator at Tower B17 must be so notified. &#13;&#13;When no operator is on duty, conductors of Metra trains required to receive a TGBO at Elgin must ascertain from the train dispatcher that they have all required track bulletins before their train departs Elgin. &#13;&#13;The train dispatcher is to be contacted sufficiently in advance of departure time to avoid train delay should it be necessary to receive a new TGBO and track bulletins. &#13;&#13;WWD midday trains turning at Big Timber Road, beginning with train No. 2209 and continuing through train No. 2219, after making station stop will proceed west approximately one-half \(1/2\) the distance to Randall Road. &#13;&#13;EWD trains will proceed to the station platform and spot train for boarding not less than fifteen \(15\) minutes prior to scheduled departure. EWD trains using No. 2 MT will arrange to leave crosswalk clear and \(if deadheading cars\) load the second car from the east end, thereby allowing passengers to utilize the crosswalk and board the train. &#13;</span></p></body>) /Rect [ 471.118 354.001 491.118 372.001 ] /Rotate 270 /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot >>
endobj
